## THIRD-PARTY DATA

================================================================================

The file `src/dataportalen/vocabulary.json` is generated data, not source code.
It is compiled by `tools/build_vocabulary.py` from the sources below and is
redistributed here under their respective terms. The MIT License covers this
package's code; it does not override the terms of the data.

---

## DCAT-AP-SE — Myndigheten för digital förvaltning (DIGG)

Swedish and English labels for the controlled vocabularies used by the Swedish
DCAT application profile.

Source: <https://github.com/diggsweden/DCAT-AP-SE>
License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>

---

## GeoNames geographical database

Place names for the `dcterms:spatial` URIs, taken from the GeoNames bulk
exports (SE.zip and countryInfo.txt).

Source: <https://www.geonames.org/>
License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>

---

## EU Vocabularies — Publications Office of the European Union

Labels for the EU authority tables: data themes, file types, frequencies,
languages, access rights, distribution status and planned availability.

Source: <https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies>
Reuse: Commission Decision 2011/833/EU on the reuse of Commission documents
<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2011/833/oj>

---

## INSPIRE registry — European Commission

Labels for INSPIRE themes, topic categories and related code lists.

Source: <https://inspire.ec.europa.eu/registry>
Reuse: Commission Decision 2011/833/EU on the reuse of Commission documents
<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2011/833/oj>

================================================================================

No third-party data is fetched at runtime. Metadata retrieved from
dataportal.se through this package is published by its respective publishers,
each under its own license — see the `license` field on every dataset.
